WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.049
In the SCP system, uncontained anomalies are
considered especially heinous.

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:10.190
At the SCP Foundation, the dedicated operatives
who investigate and neutralize these deadly

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:16.270
aberrations are members of elite, specialized
squads known as Mobile Task Forces.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.570
These are their stories.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.570
Dun dun.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.130
Hey, that was pretty good.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.330
Someone should make a TV show about this.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.579
But I digress.

00:00:23.579 --> 00:00:28.810
MTF’s are a vital part of what keeps the
SCP Foundation up and running, and keeps the

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:32.099
public safe from all kinds of dangerous anomalies.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:36.660
MTF’s specialize in a wide variety of different
threats and can be dispatched to handle those

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.140
threats when ordinary field operatives just
won’t do.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.600
They might be a large army of militarized
on-the-ground forces, or a tiny group of highly

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.330
qualified researchers.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:51.510
It all depends on their specialty, and what
sorts of threats the task force exists to

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.510
handle.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.760
Either way, they represent the best of the
best that the Foundation has to offer.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.710
If given the opportunity to join one of these
oh-so-exclusive task forces, which would you

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.440
choose and why?

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:08.100
We posed this question to our loyal viewers
here at SCP Explained, and received as wide

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.770
and varied a number of responses as the MTF’s
themselves.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:16.420
So, without further ado, let’s get into
it and see who’s suiting up for battle,

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:21.369
brushing up on their thaumatology, or trying
to crack down on that pesky Dr. Bright once

00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:22.369
and for all.

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:24.600
[ANIMATION: Dr. Bright runs away, grinning,
while being chased by MTF Members.]

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.689
Luna Heartnet said, “Beta-7, Maz-Hatters.

00:01:25.689 --> 00:01:30.159
The cleanup and containment of biohazardous
anomalies sound like grueling work, mentally

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:34.950
and physically, but it also lines up pretty
well with my real-world skill set.”

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:39.399
Listen, one of the most important parts of
job-hunting is knowing your strengths!

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:44.130
If your strength lies with cleaning up all
kinds of supernatural gunk, goo, and slime,

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.960
then more power to you!

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.270
Grab a department-issued super-mop and get
down to it.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:55.100
Thank you for your service, a clean Foundation
is an effective Foundation.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.869
Iron Clamp said, “Mu-13 “Ghostbusters”.

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:02.950
Everyone knows how scary fighting the SCPs
that you can actually see and physically deal

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.049
with are.

00:02:04.049 --> 00:02:08.759
But imagine the steel balls it takes to go
into a scene to deal with a potentially deadly

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:12.349
SCP that you can’t do either of those things
with.

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:18.170
It would be like a much more violent version
of Paranormal Activity or Insidious but instead

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.540
you have to figure out how to deal with it.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.629
Also the idea of “Ghostbusters But With
Guns!” is just too good for me to pass.”

00:02:25.629 --> 00:02:30.080
Sounds like you’re a horror fan, so enjoy
your own personal entry into the Paranormal

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:34.549
Activity Extended Universe and try your best
not to become a ghost yourself.

00:02:34.549 --> 00:02:36.739
Who ya gonna call?

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:42.260
Yanooska_A1 said, “I would definitely want
to be a member of Epsilon-11 “Nine Tailed

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.260
Fox”.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.790
The fact that they’re only called in to
deal with a facility that has gone to complete

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:51.200
shit, and in such small teams proves that
the skill set of these troops Is astonishing.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.209
Not to mention they’re under the command
of Alpha-1 “Red right hand”, who are known

00:02:55.209 --> 00:02:57.120
as the best of the best.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.319
Also probing their skills in the game SCP:
Containment Breach, where three troops are

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:06.799
sent into a facility where some of the most
infamous SCPs have breached, such as SCP-173,

00:03:06.799 --> 00:03:11.180
SCP-049, SCP-106 and many more.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:15.110
They easily sweep through the facility, with
no casualties.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:20.280
So in my opinion, Epsilon-11 would be my go
to Task Force.”

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.719
You’ve definitely got your work cut out
for you if you want to become a member of

00:03:23.719 --> 00:03:28.870
Episolon-11 and serve the Red right hand,
but if you can hold your own against the likes

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:34.239
of the Sculpture , the Old Man , and the Plague
Doctor , then go right ahead and try!

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:40.000
I hope you’ve got quick reflexes, an itchy
trigger finger, and can go hours without blinking.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.950
RiftZ said, “I'd proudly wear the insignia
of MTF Eta-10 "See No Evil".

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:50.310
I think visual cognitohazards is a really
interesting thing to work with.”

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:53.249
Interesting, sure, and extremely dangerous
too!

00:03:53.249 --> 00:03:58.310
Good job knowing what you want, and knowing
that what you want is to risk exposure to

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:02.030
all kinds of things that’ll make it impossible
to trust your own eyes.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:07.319
Don’t worry, we’ve heard working with
Eta-10 is a lot like a game of Marco, Polo!

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:11.680
Only if you get it wrong, you break your brain,
die, and unleash unspeakable destruction on

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.560
countless innocent people.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:20.620
The Drum Major said, “Definitely MTF Alpha-9
"Last Hope" I've always loved the more human/friendly

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:25.360
anomalies and feel that even the more hostile
sentient entities have some sort of kindness

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:28.970
within them that can be shown if given time.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:33.560
Being able to work along side these friendly
entities to help people would be amazing.”

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.660
That’s so sweet!

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:39.669
So instead of just containing anomalies, you’d
like to have them as your coworkers!

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:44.330
It’s a pretty impressive team you’d be
joining, one that includes the likes of Iris

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:50.740
Thompson, SCP-4051 - also known as “Your
Friendly Neighborhood Keter” - and the shadowy

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:53.730
icon of crime-fighting we call The Specter.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:58.410
But there’s no need to be intimidated, I’m
sure you have your own strengths to bring

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.900
to the table too.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:04.620
Maybe you always get everyone’s coffee order
right, or you’re great at giving pep talks.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.860
Whatever it is, you’ll be a great addition
to the team.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:12.340
Lemon Demon Danganronpa - hell of a name you
have there - said, “It would be interesting

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:17.070
for me to be part of MTF Omega-9, also known
as the Scrubs.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:21.220
For context, they are a group of gamers who
got trapped in a lobby of Quake and now help

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.590
out the Foundation.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:27.490
While being stuck in a game would have some
psychological consequences, it would be fun

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:33.210
to 360 no-scope the competition and other
SCPs who dare stand in my way!”

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:37.380
Why settle for being a Twitch streamer or
a professional in the world of e-sports, when

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:41.580
you could just leave your earthly life behind
completely and spend the rest of your days

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.330
in a world of pixels and non-stop action?

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:48.820
You’ll miss your friends and family, sure,
but don’t think too hard about that part.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.599
The rest of it sounds pretty poggers.

00:05:50.599 --> 00:05:52.240
Do people still say that?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.720
Don’t tell me, I don’t want to know.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:58.560
TheRagingAtom said, “This isn’t even a
contest.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:02.720
I’d go with MTF Sigma-3, the Bibliographers.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:08.080
Of course, not until after the whole library
invasion thing had cooled off and they reorganized.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:13.090
It’s just the closest you could get in the
foundation to recreational anomalous usage,

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.330
which is awesome.

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:19.180
Who knows, maybe I’ll sacrifice everything
I hold dear to become a type blue”

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.280
Smart move waiting for the action to cool
off first.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:25.310
If you end up becoming a type blue, let us
know!

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:29.639
I need a magic act for my nephew’s birthday
party, and he said last year’s Amazing Melvin

00:06:29.639 --> 00:06:35.389
pulling a rabbit out of a hat wasn’t cool
enough for his sixth-grade friends.

00:06:35.389 --> 00:06:43.970
Mannequin Skywalker said, “Honestly, going
to say MTF Lambda-14 (One-Star reviewers).

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:47.849
I've got a lot of experience in retail, in
many different positions.

00:06:47.849 --> 00:06:52.159
So I think I'd fit in there with being able
to tell what seems anomalous or potentially

00:06:52.159 --> 00:06:58.760
how to deal with a retail oriented SCP, including...*shudders*
a Karen Class.”

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:03.620
After working in retail, I’m sure you’ve
seen horrors that would put the findings of

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.120
the SCP Foundation to shame.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:09.740
After you’ve dealt with unruly customers
picking a fight about coupons 20 minutes after

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:13.190
closing time, there’s nothing you can’t
handle.

00:07:13.190 --> 00:07:17.419
Tor the Jackal said, “I'd go with Zeta-9
"Mole Rats".

00:07:17.419 --> 00:07:21.139
I love enclosed spaces, especially those underground.

00:07:21.139 --> 00:07:24.860
If given the opportunity I would definitely
join Zeta-9.”

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:27.090
Are you sure you’re not part mole?

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.210
Groundhog, maybe?

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:34.220
I’ve never met anyone who “loves” enclosed
spaces, let alone underground ones, but I

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:38.590
also got kicked out of my local spelunking
team for crying too much so maybe that’s

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:39.740
just me.

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:45.819
Sharky Reynolds said, “I'd go for MTF Lambda-5
(White Rabbits), and I would use my training

00:07:45.819 --> 00:07:50.729
to determine if the terrible new songs coming
out these days are only popular through reality

00:07:50.729 --> 00:07:55.280
warping properties or if the world is doomed
to experience bad taste.”

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.319
It’s probably anomalies.

00:07:57.319 --> 00:08:02.150
After all, everyone knows that bad music is
a brand new invention and every previous generation

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:06.590
didn’t think the exact same thing about
the new music their kids were listening to.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:11.789
Hang on, I’m being told that’s absolutely
what happened and that taste is subjective?

00:08:11.789 --> 00:08:12.789
Sounds fake.

00:08:12.789 --> 00:08:17.340
Besides, there’s got to be a supernatural
explanation for “What Does the Fox Say?”,

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.580
I won’t hear otherwise.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:24.659
BananaOne said, “Zeta-9, "Mole Rats" I gotta
respect this task force since they have the

00:08:24.659 --> 00:08:27.520
lowest survival rate when it comes to their
missions.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.560
Besides, I like how their insignia was made
with a design of a gas mask.”

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:34.719
We’ve got another volunteer for the Mole
Rats!

00:08:34.719 --> 00:08:37.880
What is it with you guys and dangerous underground
situations?

00:08:37.880 --> 00:08:42.450
It’s a cool insignia, sure, but there’s
a reason it’s a gas mask.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:45.300
You’ll need to wear a GAS MASK.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.290
Good luck to you, I guess.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:52.670
Nicktwolf discusses said, “For me, it's
kind of a tie between two groups.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:56.410
I would love to be on MTF Eta-11 ("Savage
Beasts").

00:08:56.410 --> 00:09:01.000
I know I'm not 100% deaf and working on learning
sign language.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.251
Being part of a group where I felt like I
belonged and might be excepted would be a

00:09:05.251 --> 00:09:06.399
dream come true.

00:09:06.399 --> 00:09:11.480
If I couldn't get into there, MTF Sigma-3
("Bibliographers") would be amazing.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:16.390
The idea of possibly spending time doing research
and gather info in the Library would be a

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:18.090
great experience.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:22.470
And in possible down time, all of those books
that are waiting to be read.”

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:24.260
That’s a great reason!

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:29.279
The Savage Beasts would be lucky to have you,
and you deserve to work with a team that understands

00:09:29.279 --> 00:09:32.240
and appreciates your unique strengths.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:36.310
Maybe you could split your time between the
two and moonlight as a Bibliographer!

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:40.190
EternalTribute said, “I'd choose Tau-5 "Samsara".

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:45.240
I already feel basically emotionless so it
would have zero impact on me and I like the

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:49.560
idea of immortality and being a cyborg (I
love technology).

00:09:49.560 --> 00:10:00.510
However, my alternative would be the Debuggers
or Skynet because I am decent with computers.”

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:07.060
Fabian Roberts said, “MTF Beta-777 ("Hecate's
Spear") Bc I think it’d be interesting to

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:11.450
look for knowledge about the occult rituals
and how to stop them!

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.680
Especially in instances where an SCP was involved.”

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:17.740
Specializing in thaumaturgical ritual analysis,
eh?

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:24.260
It’s the closest thing out there to joining
a literal wizard army, so I can see the appeal.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:29.010
Just be careful, the world of thaumatology
attracts the attention of forces you don’t

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:31.920
want putting a magical target on your back.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:36.240
Unlike the aforementioned Amazing Melvin,
these guys are doing this stuff for real,

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:41.779
and they’ll do a lot worse than sawing you
in half if you slip up on the job.

00:10:41.779 --> 00:10:47.800
Mr.Pixel said, “I would probably want to
be a part of MTF Epsilon-9, the fire eaters.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:52.300
After all, who can say no to the alluring
destructive power of fire.

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:56.110
And its not a war crime if i roast mostly
anomalous creatures instead of humans.”

00:10:56.110 --> 00:11:00.820
For the second time in this video, I say…Are
you okay, buddy?

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.920
Maybe you should have a glass of water.

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:07.730
You can’t use it to roast your enemies alive,
but it’ll help you settle down.

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:11.160
https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/414ZVy9kDVL.jpg]
Nick O’Tein said, “"Skynet" of course.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:16.480
The internet is a vast ocean containing both
everything and nothing, thus giving me something

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:20.450
to do for the rest of time, or at least until
the world ends.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:24.899
Plus, what better excuse than being a member
of "Skynet" would I have to watch you guys

00:11:24.899 --> 00:11:26.110
all day?”

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:27.860
Now you’re talking!

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:32.230
When you’re not tracking sentient malware
or the influence of the Archon Lord , you

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:35.510
can spend your time watching more videos from
SCP Explained!

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:40.519
That’s the perfect way to unwind after a
long day of scouring the web for old gods

00:11:40.519 --> 00:11:44.339
and, I don’t know, an iPhone app that knows
when you’re going to die?

00:11:44.339 --> 00:11:45.339
You’re the web expert, not me.

00:11:45.339 --> 00:11:49.190
Hey, maybe you could teach me how to make
a TikTok!

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:54.100
Incidentally, we do actually have a TikTok
now at SCPExplainedOfficial.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.829
Go check it out after the video!

00:11:55.829 --> 00:11:58.779
Applethree3D said, “Beta 7.

00:11:58.779 --> 00:12:04.019
I'm a bio chemist in real life so this would
just go well with my skillsets.

00:12:04.019 --> 00:12:08.360
Working with anomalous biohazard clean up
sounds like grueling mental and physical work.”

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:10.880
Didn’t know we had biochemists watching
us!

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:11.880
That’s awesome!

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:15.950
You’re probably overqualified to clean up
biohazardous anomalous material, but dress

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.560
for the job you want!

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:21.949
By which I mean, you should probably wear
a HAZMAT suit and some heavy-duty goggles.

00:12:21.949 --> 00:12:26.230
Who knows what kind of radioactive slime and
monster snot you’ll be wiping up.

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:30.930
Jei the monk of cherry trees said, “If I
was asked to join any of the MTF teams, most

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:36.250
likely after looking into them, would be:
MTF Theta-4, the Gardeners.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:41.860
Seeing that many MTF teams usually follow
certain protocols, Gardeners seem to situated

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:49.110
around very flora based SCP's, usually in
sites or locations of known flora based SCP's,

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:54.920
either mitigating the effects, securing or
researching potential ''sprouts'' of SCP's.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.660
Maybe some woodworkers skills might come handy
helping the team.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:04.420
Though I thoroughly wonder if SCP foundation
would trust a man in a MTF team called Gardeners,

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.290
whom has a bonsai plum tree growing from their
head.”

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:12.760
Oh, that’s so nice, you must have a hell
of a green thumb- wait, I’m sorry.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:14.339
What was that last part?

00:13:14.339 --> 00:13:17.320
Bonsai plum tree growing from your head?

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:21.010
For the third, and hopefully final time: Are
you okay?

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:23.550
Blink twice if you’re in danger.

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:28.970
James Harrold said, “Definitely MTF Gamma
13, Asimov's Lawbringers, they're the group

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:33.290
in charge of dealing with Anderson Robotics,
who's the most interesting group outside of

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.850
maybe the Church of the Broken God to me.”

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:41.221
Anderson Robotics has been a cybernetic thorn
in the Foundation’s side since 2007, with

00:13:41.221 --> 00:13:46.060
influence all throughout the Pacific Northwest
of the United States, as well as branches

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:48.949
in New Mexico, Arizona, and Louisiana.

00:13:48.949 --> 00:13:53.790
They’re an elusive group, and while they’re
unlikely to attack the Foundation directly,

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:59.250
their use of science and magic in one mysterious
package is definitely something to keep an

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:00.250
eye on.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:06.700
Fish Hsif said, “I’d have to go with upsilon
23, art critics.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:11.139
I’m usually drawing or painting so I’m
down to get my hands dirty dealing with anomalous

00:14:11.139 --> 00:14:12.139
art.

00:14:12.139 --> 00:14:15.399
And I love sloths”
You like drawing and painting, so naturally,

00:14:15.399 --> 00:14:17.670
you’d like to work with anomalous art.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:19.029
Makes sense.

00:14:19.029 --> 00:14:24.949
You might want to steer clear of any art depicting
SCP-2774 though, if you want to continue loving

00:14:24.949 --> 00:14:26.100
sloths.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:29.880
That thing will ruin sloths for you faster
than you can say “Nowhere is safe.

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:31.600
In the corner of my eye, it's just…

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:32.600
Staring…

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.149
I don't know, I don't know!”

00:14:34.149 --> 00:14:40.800
Charles Watson said, “MTF Eta-5 ("Jäeger
Bombers") sounds exactly like my dream job.

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:45.190
Bombing runs in something like a C-130 is
already something I'm interested in, and getting

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:49.220
to fight what are essentially Kaiju monsters
makes it ten times better.”

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.220
Oh.

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:54.290
You said fighting?

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.790
Bombing runs?

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:59.510
I grossly misunderstood what Eta-5 is responsible
for.

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:04.940
I’ll just put this bottle of Jägermeister
away and get back to work…

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:08.330
Final Advance said, “MTF Eta-11, Savage
Beasts.

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:13.579
I get triggered by even non anomalous noises
easily so dealing with audio based cognito

00:15:13.579 --> 00:15:18.420
hazards where noise discipline and actively
shutting out sounds is perfect for me.”

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:22.550
If you hate sounds, I guess there’s no better
workplace than somewhere where you have to

00:15:22.550 --> 00:15:24.850
avoid hearing things at all costs.

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:30.199
You’ll be facing off against trumpets that
can collapse walls, an anomalous chord progression,

00:15:30.199 --> 00:15:35.410
and even a corrupted Beatles song, so make
sure you get some really good-quality noise-canceling

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.949
headphones though, or you’ll be in for a
rude awakening.

00:15:38.949 --> 00:15:43.630
Alexander Berry said, “Bright-99 "oh no
you don't!".

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:48.470
As a way to contain them more efficiently,
I'd have them set up some form of comedic

00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:52.579
entertainment to be broadcasted throughout
the foundation to boost morale while keeping

00:15:52.579 --> 00:15:54.389
the Bright's entertained.

00:15:54.389 --> 00:15:59.230
Of course to be safe we'll keep an eye on
all items they have access to and run the

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:02.660
broadcast through a filter to get rid of possible
cognitohazards.”

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:05.149
“Oh no you don’t” is right!

00:16:05.149 --> 00:16:10.230
If you’re a regular viewer of this channel,
or a fan of the designated page on the SCP

00:16:10.230 --> 00:16:14.800
wiki, you know that there are more things
Dr. Bright is not allowed to do than there

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.500
are things he is.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:21.150
It’ll take some pretty great comedic entertainment
to keep Bright occupied, I don’t think you

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:24.860
can just throw on Spongebob or Cocomelon and
call it a day.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:29.560
Dr. Bright is way too attracted to real-life
chaos to be distracted by television, though

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:31.610
it’s a nice enough idea.

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:35.630
Or, wait…are you suggesting we give Dr.
Bright his own tv show?

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:39.630
That’s too much power, you can’t let him
on the airwaves!

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:43.290
He’ll have half the Foundation quacking
like a duck and make the other half’s heads

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:45.720
explode before you can change the channel!

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:48.779
Sorry, your request to join Bright-99 has
been DENIED.

00:16:48.779 --> 00:16:55.100
Kirt Gamer said, “I would proudly put the
insignia of MTF Theta-90 In my shoulder knowing

00:16:55.100 --> 00:17:01.230
that I have defended humanity, especially
children, from the anomalous mathematics problems.

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:06.090
I will even happily lay down my life to protect
children from trauma, stress, and especially

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:12.330
depression that anomalous math can do I think
math in its entirety is even anomalous, let

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:17.690
us rally together people to ask the 05 council
to contain math entirely due to its anomalous

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:20.620
ability to make anyone cry and be depressed.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:24.260
I hope my work can bring a smile to the children
that I have defended”

00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:26.690
This brought a tear to my eye.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:31.450
Thank you, Kirt, for your willingness to fight
against the scourge that is simple mathematics.

00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:35.020
With your hard work, children all over the
world will never need to hear about Billy

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:38.810
buying 30 watermelons and 22 apples ever again.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:44.280
Now go check out “SCP Elite Mobile Task
Force Explained” and “SCP Global Occult

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:48.640
Coalition Explained” for more specialized
groups at the SCP Foundation!

